      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): reply session init fails under rapid consecutive turns",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes transient `reply session initialization conflicted` failures by replacing the single stale-snapshot retry in reply-session initialization with a bounded 4-attempt budget.\n\n## Details\n\n`commitReplySessionInitialization` uses an expected-revision guard. Under rapid same-session turns, another writer can advance the session-store revision between snapshot and commit more than once. The previous code retried once, then surfaced the conflict to the user.\n\nThis keeps the same snapshot, commit, locking, and failure semantics. It only increases the bounded retry budget for stale snapshots.\n\n## Validation\n\nAdded `src/auto-reply/reply/session-init-retry-budget.test.ts`, which uses the real file-backed `loadReplySessionInitializationSnapshot` and `commitReplySessionInitialization` functions:\n\n```text\nold budget (2 attempts) throws under a 3-writer burst\nnew budget (4 attempts) succeeds under the identical 3-writer burst\n```\n\nChecked locally:\n\n```text\nnpx vitest run src/auto-reply/reply/session-init-retry-budget.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session.test.ts extensions/telegram/src/polling-session.test.ts\nTest Files  3 passed (3)\nTests       201 passed (201)\n```\n\nAlso checked:\n\n```text\nnpx oxlint src/auto-reply/reply/session.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-init-retry-budget.test.ts\nnpx oxfmt --check src/auto-reply/reply/session-init-retry-budget.test.ts\nnpx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.core.json\n```\n\n`tsc` has no new errors; the existing `TS4058` in `src/secrets/config-io.ts` reproduces on `main`.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis is a small mitigation for transient same-session write races. It does not replace the related root-cause work in #98416 or #98835.\n",
